{"amendments":[{"body":"Update the shrimp provenance path so omitted optional fields fall back to the runtime defaults before formatting and range checks. Today `ShrimpPreset::lookup_param_value` returns `None` for optional fields such as `body_*`, `juvenile_to_subadult_days`, `base_clutch_size`, and `min_clutch_condition` when the TOML omits them (`crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs:304-317`, `crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs:476-502`), but `shrimp_preset_to_params` later injects real defaults from `ShrimpRuntimeParams::default()` (`crates/tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs:550-597`). That makes provenance on code-defined shrimp defaults effectively write-only: `format_param()` and `check_ranges()` never surface it even though the runtime uses a concrete value.","rationale":"This misses the bead’s code-defined-defaults requirement and silently drops provenance/debug coverage for omitted optional shrimp fields."},{"body":"Make the new process-parameter formatter stop renormalizing legacy `_mg` / `_mg_total` values unless it can also show the corresponding metadata/unit, or automatically attach that derived unit. `ParamMetaPreset::format_param` currently calls `provenance_param_value()` before it checks whether any `param_meta` exists (`crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs:59-64`), and `ProcessParamsPreset::provenance_param_value` always rewrites legacy compatibility fields into reference-tank concentrations (`crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs:1144-1150`). Because the shipped default process preset intentionally has no `param_meta` (`crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs:1857-1864`) but still stores `aob_k_tan_mg = 0.5` (`crates/tank_data/data/process/default.toml:31`), the debug helper can print a transformed value like `0.025` with no unit/source context, which is misleading.","rationale":"The formatter is supposed to make provenance/debug output clearer; for the common legacy preset case it currently changes the number without enough context to interpret it."},{"body":"Tighten `ProcessParamsPreset::validate` to reject `shrimp_juvenile_maturation_days <= 0`. The validator only rejects negative values today (`crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs:1334-1387`), but scenario materialization immediately splits that legacy total into stage durations (`crates/tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs:546-564`; `crates/tank_core/src/types/biology.rs:342-354`) and runtime invariants require both resulting fields to be strictly positive (`crates/tank_core/src/invariants.rs:316-323`). A custom process preset with `shrimp_juvenile_maturation_days = 0.0` will therefore load successfully and only fail later when the engine is stepped.","rationale":"This is a loader/runtime mismatch: invalid preset data is accepted up front and only rejected much later by the engine."}],"summary":"Reviewed the cumulative diff with focus on the provenance/preset loader changes, read the key implementation files end-to-end, and ran `cargo test -p tank_data`, `cargo test -p tank_scenarios`, `cargo test -p tank_harness`, and `cargo test -p tank_core`. I found three remaining correctness gaps: code-defined shrimp defaults still lose provenance, the new process formatter can misreport legacy values without metadata context, and zero legacy shrimp maturation days pass preset validation even though runtime invariants reject them."}